{# analyze.j2 — AI grammar and quality check for resume content.
   Expected context keys:
     content       (str)       — full text of the resume section or entire resume to check
     section_label (str)       — human-readable label, e.g. "Professional Summary" or "Experience"
     tone          (str)       — desired tone: "professional" | "technical" | "creative"
     language      (str)       — BCP-47 code of the content language, e.g. "en"
     checks        (list[str]) — list of check types to perform, e.g. ["grammar", "consistency", "clarity"]
#}
You are a professional resume editor and grammar expert.

Analyse the following resume {{ section_label }} for quality issues.

Language: {{ language }}
Expected tone: {{ tone }}
Checks to perform: {{ checks | join(', ') }}

---
{{ content }}
---

Provide a structured analysis with the following format:

ISSUES:
- [severity: HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW] [type] Description of the issue and suggested fix.
(List each issue on its own line. If no issues found, write "No issues found.")

OVERALL_SCORE: [0-100]

SUMMARY:
One sentence summarising the overall quality and the most important improvement needed.

Output ONLY the structured analysis above, no additional commentary:
